* text=auto eol=lf
*.raimodel binary

# THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md is generated by `cargo about` from `about.hbs`, and CI
# regenerates it and diffs. That gate only holds if the committed bytes are the
# bytes a Linux checkout produces, so the file must be LF like everything else
# — which `* text=auto eol=lf` above already guarantees. It is called out here
# only to record that it needs no exception: an earlier `-text` entry was added
# in the belief that upstream license texts contributed CRLF lines, and
# regenerating from an LF template produces a file with none.

# Windows batch files must reach cmd.exe with CRLF: with LF-only line endings
# cmd mis-parses block structure (a nested `exit /b N` silently returns 0).
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf

# Shell scripts must reach a Unix shell with LF. `* text=auto eol=lf` above
# already does this, but these are the files where a stray CRLF is fatal rather
# than cosmetic — `#!/usr/bin/env bash\r` makes the kernel look for an
# interpreter named "bash\r" and report a confusing "no such file or directory"
# against a script that plainly exists — so they are declared explicitly.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.command text eol=lf
*.desktop text eol=lf

# NOTE: .gitattributes cannot make a file executable. The executable bit lives
# in the index, and a shell script checked out without it cannot be
# double-clicked or run as ./script. Set it once per script with:
#   git update-index --chmod=+x launchers/rai-studio.sh launchers/rai-studio.command
# and verify with `git ls-files -s launchers/` (mode must read 100755).
